# Experiment run outputs are generated: new runs route to runs/<target>/<suite>/ (see CLAUDE.md).
# Any legacy per-experiment runs/ dir is regenerable and never tracked.
merlin/experiments/**/runs/
# Transient agentic-experiment workspaces: per-run bwrap workspaces full of absolute symlinks +
# live-written state (never want these tracked; durable artifacts live in runs/ and reports/).
**/_qa_ws/
# cross-arm verilator slot semaphore (runtime only)
/tmp/oscar_merlin_veril_slots/

# Firecrawl tool-state (web-scrape cache; not repo content)
/.firecrawl/


# External machine-specific dep config — NEVER commit the active files (real paths).
# Only .env.example (the template) is tracked. See merlin.common.paths.ext_path().
/.env
/config.json
/config.local.json
!/.env.example

# Per-experiment tooling-path env (real machine paths, all arms) — only the .example is tracked.
**/experiment.env
!**/experiment.env.example

# General ignore
tmp
.compat_lib/

# ── Benchmark ANSWER KEYS — never tracked anywhere (public repo: github.com/ucb-bar/merlin) ──
# Graded answers (golden outputs + required instruction coverage) and the held-out HIDDEN sets. These
# are the answers an agent is graded against; committing them defeats the benchmark AND enables
# cheating. Regenerable from the tracked generators + oracle; the public CONTRACT (capsule.interface.mlir
# + capsule.yaml + MANIFEST.yaml, outside hidden/) stays tracked. Global — covers capsule_bench,
# gemmini_perf_bench, agent_bench, and any future benchmark dir.
**/golden.yaml
**/golden_*.yaml
**/expected_instruction_coverage.yaml
**/hidden/
# Externalized capsule weights are large regenerable binaries AND, for a whole-model capsule, the
# thing the golden was computed from. The rule existed only in merlin/contract/capsules/.gitignore,
# so it protected nothing under artifacts/, out/, or harness/full_public_capsules/ — where 11 weight
# blobs were surfacing as untracked. Make it global, like every other rule in this section.
**/*.safetensors
**/*.safetensors.manifest.json

# targetgen_evals grading rubrics + the declared holdout. A `golden/` DIRECTORY is an answer surface
# (check_no_answer_keys.py matches it as a path component, as it already did for `hidden/`); the two
# files the method's own prompt hands it are re-included below as declared stimulus.
/merlin/experiments/targetgen_evals/datasets/*/golden/**
!/merlin/experiments/targetgen_evals/datasets/*/golden/expected_contract.yaml
!/merlin/experiments/targetgen_evals/datasets/*/golden/expected_dialect_features.yaml

# dse-guidance case study: the generated tables are re-included by the negation above, but these two
# subtrees are session working material (slide triage, positioning memos, one-off validation scripts)
# that no tool produces or reads -- they are not artifacts.
/out/artifacts/dse-guidance/case_study/final_presentation_pass/**
/out/artifacts/dse-guidance/case_study/manual_validation/**
# Point-in-time agent run notes: addressed to the operator, and they link private vaults / accounts.
/out/artifacts/perf-bench/*/AUTONOMOUS_RUN_SUMMARY.md
/out/artifacts/capsule-bench/*/AGENTIC_AB_RUNBOOK.md
# llvm-lit writes a per-suite timing cache next to the tests on every run. It is scheduling state, not
# a test input, and it reappears the moment anyone runs the suite -- so without this it shows up as an
# untracked file in every session and eventually gets swept into someone's commit.
merlin/tests/data/lit/.lit_test_times.txt

# Voyager head-to-head: the comparative analysis stays internal. This repo is public, and these three
# carry our positioning against another group's published work -- including a defect in their public
# release and the paper claims we intend to make from it. The reproducible half of the experiment
# (bridge, harnesses, concession register) stays tracked; only the analysis is held back. Copies live
# under out/artifacts/presentation/merlin_retrospective_20260911/.
/merlin/experiments/voyager_h2h/LESSONS.md
/merlin/experiments/voyager_h2h/STATUS.md
/merlin/experiments/voyager_h2h/PLANE_B.md

